{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011ChAzVE9HRRVVVWJ8bAvHC","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"[x] `npm run lint`, `npm run typecheck`, and `npm run test:ts` pass, and the Go build and Go tests still pass.\n\n`npx roast skill install` and `npx roast skill status` now work in the TypeScript CLI. All ten checklist items are done and committed, and every gate passes: lint, typecheck, `test:ts` (936 passing), `go build`, and the full `npm test` (Go and launcher tests).\n\n**What's new:**\n- **`src/skill/assets.ts`**: `SKILL_FILES`, with one import per file from `internal/skill/assets/roast/` (today only `SKILL.md`). Its test also fails if a file in that directory has no import.\n- **`src/skill/skill.ts`**: `inspect`, `install`, `installationTargets` and `lookPath`, ported from the Go package. Home, `CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR`, `XDG_CONFIG_HOME` and `PATH` all come from the passed-in environment, and a missing `HOME` is an error, as in Go.\n- **`src/cli/skill.ts`**: the `skill` group (no subcommand prints help, exit 0), `install`, `status` and `skillTargets`, registered in `src/cli/commands.ts`. `--dir` wins over `--global`. Outside a repository without either flag, both commands are a usage error (exit 2).\n\n**One change from the spec:** it says `export let lookPath`, but tests can't reassign an ESM `let` export. I used the same pattern as `terminalHooks` instead: a mutable `skillHooks.lookPath` with a `lookPath` export that calls it.\n\n**Testing:** several tests passed on their first run, because the Go port already included the symlink guards, the toplevel lookup, the usage-error wrapping and the `--dir`-over-`--global` order. To show those tests can actually fail, I disabled each piece in turn, confirmed the matching tests went red, and restored the code.\n\nTwo git-runner tests in `test/git/git.ts` (the fake-git pid ones) timed out once while the machine was busy. Three clean reruns all passed, so they look flaky, and they're unrelated to this ticket.\n\nI added these points to `AGENTS.md`: the hooks-object pattern, the one-import-per-file rule for skill assets, and why skill tests blank `CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR` (the shared isolated test env sets it, which counts as Claude Code being installed). My notes for this attempt are in `.redeye/notes.md`, not committed."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":305,"cache_read_input_tokens":118105,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":305},"output_tokens":777,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"91e5653d-6039-4c60-b920-40dca47b5a0a","uuid":"02c03ad3-0007-4eb6-a59d-9d09aa3927bc","timestamp":"2026-11-18T20:03:40.874Z","request_id":"req_011ChAzVDveJTh1nupzkXcVG"}
